# init.txt: commands a dedicated server runs once at its start, one a line,
# as if typed at its console (docs/dedicated_server.md, "Commands"). Copy
# this file to init.txt in the data folder (server.init_file), and take the
# "# " off the lines you want. Lines starting with # or ; are comments.
#
# Settings are better given in config.toml or as HALO_* variables; these are
# for what changes from one start to the next.

# The rotation, replacing server.rotation (and written to it):
# sv_rotation_set bloodgulch:ctf, sidewinder:team_slayer+score=50, hangemhigh:king_moving
# sv_rotation_add prisoner:slayer+time=10
# sv_rotation_begin 2

# The game's name, players and notice (sv_set of the server.* settings):
# sv_name My server
# sv_maxplayers 12
# sv_motd Welcome. Be nice; admins are watching.
# sv_public 1
# sv_password secret

# Any setting the server lists in sv_settings:
# sv_set server.lobby_seconds 20
# sv_set server.empty_seconds 60

# A first game other than the rotation's, which goes on after it:
# sv_map bloodgulch ctf_classic

# The state of the server, in the log:
# sv_status

# The game's own console commands run too, with the owner's role.
